# WebUI `src/` directory structure

Alias: `@/` → `webui/src/`.

## Tree

```text
webui/src/
├── main.tsx                 # entry: mount, i18n, global CSS
├── App.tsx                  # boot / auth; HashRouter + AppLayout when ready
├── stores/                  # Zustand (ui chrome, session badges)
├── routes/                  # URL ↔ ShellRoute + useShellNavigate + HashChangeSync
├── layouts/                 # app chrome — see `layouts/README.md`
│   ├── AppLayout.tsx        # thin composer
│   ├── constants.ts
│   ├── chrome/              # HostChrome, sidebar, main, dialogs
│   └── hooks/               # useAppLayoutModel + domain hooks
├── globals.css
│
├── pages/                   # route-level pages (one folder per feature)
│   ├── index.ts
│   └── <page>/
│       ├── index.ts         # export { XxxPage }
│       ├── XxxPage.tsx      # data / state / handlers + compose UI
│       ├── xxx-ui.tsx       # optional large presentational split
│       └── components/      # page-private UI only
│
├── components/              # shared business UI (2+ consumers)
│   ├── ui/                  # atomic primitives (shadcn / Radix)
│   ├── shell/               # sidebar, session lists, chrome dialogs
│   ├── thread/              # chat / session domain (+ activity/)
│   ├── markdown/            # MarkdownText / CodeBlock pipeline
│   └── settings/            # settings-domain shared chrome
│
├── hooks/                   # reusable hooks by domain — see `hooks/` layout below
├── lib/                     # no JSX — see `lib/` layout below
├── providers/               # React context providers
├── i18n/                    # i18n init + locales/<lang>/common.json
├── tests/                   # Vitest + Testing Library
├── types/                   # ambient *.d.ts
└── workers/                 # Web Workers
```

## `hooks/` layout

```text
hooks/
├── sessions/       # list / history / stream / pickers
├── skills/         # skills list + hub catalog
├── settings/       # settings, usage, workspaces, provider models
├── channels/       # Feishu / Weixin
├── automations/    # cron jobs
├── ui/             # theme, sidebar, composer helpers
└── index.ts        # re-exports (prefer `@/hooks/<domain>`)
```

Import from domain barrels (`@/hooks/sessions`, `@/hooks/settings`). Page-private hooks stay under `pages/<page>/`.

## `lib/` layout

```text
lib/
├── apis/           # REST / WS / bootstrap HTTP
├── configs/        # feature flags & runtime/host config
├── constants/      # static maps (e.g. provider-brand)
├── utils/          # pure helpers (cn, format, media, …)
├── types/          # shared TypeScript types
└── chat/           # session/message-domain logic
```

| Path | Put here | Do not put here |
|------|----------|-----------------|
| `lib/apis/` | HTTP/WS clients, fetch helpers | UI, pure formatters |
| `lib/configs/` | env/build flags, host runtime adapters | API call implementations |
| `lib/constants/` | static tables / brand maps | logic with side effects |
| `lib/utils/` | general pure helpers | chat-turn domain pipelines |
| `lib/types/` | shared DTOs split by domain (`message`, `settings`, `protocol`, …) | runtime code |
| `lib/chat/` | activity timeline, tool traces, display scrubbers | generic `cn` / date format |

Import from category paths (`@/lib/apis/api`, `@/lib/utils/format`). `@/lib/utils` / `@/lib/types` resolve via folder barrels.

## Layer responsibilities

| Path | Put here | Do not put here |
|------|----------|-----------------|
| `pages/<page>/` | page entry, orchestration, `components/` used only by this page | atomic Button/Dialog; multi-page business blocks |
| `layouts/` | app chrome (`AppLayout`; `chrome/` UI + `hooks/` model — see `layouts/README.md`) | feature pages; route URL helpers |
| `routes/` | URL ↔ `ShellRoute`, `useShellNavigate`, `HashChangeSync` | layout JSX; feature UI |
| `stores/` | Zustand chrome / session-badge state | server session lists / WS client |
| `components/ui/` | Button, Dialog, Input, Sheet, … | business copy / API logic |
| `components/shell/` | sidebar, chat list, chrome dialogs, language switcher | chat bubbles / markdown |
| `components/thread/` | chat surface, messages, activity, file preview | settings forms; sidebar |
| `components/markdown/` | MarkdownText, CodeBlock renderer | page-private widgets |
| `components/settings/` | settings-domain shared chrome | one-off page widgets |
| `hooks/` | domain-grouped reusable `useXxx` (`@/hooks/sessions`, …) | page-private helpers (`pages/<page>/useXxx.ts`) |
| `lib/` | categorized modules above | React components / JSX |
| `providers/` | global Context | ordinary feature UI |
| `i18n/` | locale JSON + i18n bootstrap | business logic |
| `tests/` | `*.test.ts(x)` | production code |

## File size

- Prefer **≤ ~350 lines** per file.
- Over that: split page shell / UI sections / hooks / helpers.
- Prefer extraction over growing mega-files; thin re-exports only for migration compatibility.
- Legacy giants (`App.tsx`, `SettingsView.tsx`): new work should land in `pages/` or `components/<domain>/`, not keep appending.

## Placement checklist

1. Primitive control? → `components/ui`
2. App chrome / layout frame? → `layouts/`
3. URL / navigate helpers? → `routes/`
4. App layout or ≥2 pages import UI? → `components/` (domain subfolder OK)
5. Only this page? → `pages/<page>/components/`
6. No JSX, testable pure logic? → `lib/` (`apis` / `configs` / `constants` / `utils` / `types` / `chat`)
7. Reusable React state logic? → `hooks/<domain>/` (or `stores/` for cross-tree chrome)
8. Only this page's data lifecycle? → `pages/<page>/useXxx.ts`

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — page-only widget in shared components/
import { FeishuQrPanel } from "@/components/FeishuQrPanel";

// ✅ GOOD — colocated with the only consumer
import { FeishuQrPanel } from "@/pages/channels/components/FeishuQrPanel";

// ✅ GOOD — atomic / shared business
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { MessageBubble } from "@/components/MessageBubble";
```

## Page folder convention

```text
pages/channels/
  index.ts                 # export { ChannelsPage } from "./ChannelsPage"
  ChannelsPage.tsx
  components/              # channels-only
```

Public import: `import { ChannelsPage } from "@/pages/channels"`.

Do not add full page implementations under `components/settings/`.
